\ Ollama's REST API over lib/http.telic's curl subprocess: completions and
\ chats, plain or streamed to a handler as the replies arrive; tool calling
\ with registered handlers and a conversation loop that runs the tools a reply
\ asks for; embeddings as a matrix; the model store (list, show, pull, push,
\ copy, delete, create, running models) and blobs. Requests and replies are
\ frames, sent and parsed as JSON, so a JSON true or false is the symbol :1 or
\ :0. Native-only: needs start-process and the curl binary, and shasum for
\ blob digests.

"http" load-library

\ the API's root, the server on this machine at ollama's default port; assign another to reach another server
"http://localhost:11434/api/" to ollama-url

\ a chat message: the role a symbol or string (:system :user :assistant :tool), the content a string, or a frame sent as its JSON text
: ollama-message ( role content -- message )
	| role content |

	content frame? if content frame>json to content then
	{ :role role "{0}" format :content content } ;

\ the text a failed request throws: the status and the server's :error when the body holds one, else the body
: ollama-error ( status body -- text )
	| status body |

	( body json>frame :error @ ) catch if drop body trim then to detail
	detail size 0 = if status "ollama: HTTP {0}" format exit then
	status detail "ollama: HTTP {1}: {0}" format ; internal

\ one request to an endpoint, the body a frame sent as JSON or null; answers the reply parsed from JSON, null for an empty body. A status outside 2xx throws the server's error
: ollama-request ( method endpoint body -- reply )
	| method endpoint body |

	body null? if null else body frame>json then to payload
	method ollama-url endpoint + [ "Content-Type: application/json" ] payload http-request to response

	response@status to status
	response@body trim to text
	status 200 < status 300 >= or if status text ollama-error throw then

	text size 0 = if null else text json>frame then ; internal

\ a stream's lines read as they arrive, each reply handed to the handler and kept; the last line is the status curl appends, and a reply carrying :error is kept back as the failure instead of being handled
: ollama-read-stream ( process handler -- replies status failure )
	| process handler |

	[ ] to replies
	null to failure
	null to pending

	begin process@out read-line to line line null? not while
		pending null? not if
			pending trim size 0 > if
				pending json>frame to reply
				reply :error has? if
					pending to failure
				else
					reply handler execute
					replies reply add-last! drop
				then
			then
		then
		line to pending
	repeat

	replies pending null? if 0 else pending string>number then failure ; internal

\ stream an endpoint: the body sent with :stream true, each reply handed to the handler ( reply -- ) as it arrives; answers every reply in order. A reply carrying :error, a status outside 2xx, or a failed transfer throws, as does the handler, the transfer abandoned
: ollama-stream ( endpoint body handler -- replies )
	| endpoint body handler |

	[ "curl" "-sS" "-N" "-X" "POST" ollama-url endpoint +
	  "-H" "Content-Type: application/json"
	  "--data-binary" body { :stream :1 } merge frame>json
	  "-w" "\n%{http_code}" ] start-process to process
	process@in close

	process handler ' ollama-read-stream 2curry catch if
		process@pid stop drop
		process@out close
		process@err close
		throw
	then
	to failure to status to replies

	process@err read trim to transfer-error
	process@out close
	process@err close
	process@pid wait 0 = not if transfer-error throw then

	failure null? not if status failure ollama-error throw then
	status 200 < status 300 >= or if status "" ollama-error throw then

	replies ; internal

\ the last of a stream's replies, which must report :status success
: ollama-final-status ( replies -- reply )
	| replies |

	replies size 0 = if "ollama: the stream ended with no reply" throw then

	replies last to reply
	reply :status "" @or "success" = not if "ollama: the stream ended before status success" throw then

	reply ; internal

\ === completions and chats ===

\ a completion of the prompt by the model, unstreamed: options a frame of the request's other fields (:system :format :images :options :think …), { } for none; answers the reply, the text under :response
: ollama-generate ( model prompt options -- reply )
	| model prompt options |
	"POST" "generate" options { :model model :prompt prompt :stream :0 } merge ollama-request ;

\ a completion streamed: each reply handed to the handler ( reply -- ) as it arrives, its piece of text under :response; answers the final reply with :response the whole text
: ollama-generate-streaming ( model prompt options handler -- reply )
	| model prompt options handler |

	"generate" options { :model model :prompt prompt } merge handler ollama-stream to replies

	replies ( :response "" @or ) map "" join to text
	replies last copy text :response ! ;

\ a streamed reply's message piece added to the message gathered so far: the content and thinking joined, the images and tool calls appended, the tool name the last given
: ollama-add-piece ( message reply -- message )
	| message reply |

	reply :message { } @or to piece

	piece :content has? if message message@content piece@content + :content ! drop then
	piece :thinking has? if message message :thinking "" @or piece@thinking + :thinking ! drop then
	piece :images null @or array? if message message :images [ ] @or piece@images concat :images ! drop then
	piece :tool_calls null @or array? if message message :tool_calls [ ] @or piece@tool_calls concat :tool_calls ! drop then
	piece :tool_name has? if message piece@tool_name :tool_name ! drop then

	message ; internal

\ the model's next message in a chat, unstreamed: messages an array of message frames, options a frame of the request's other fields (:tools :format :options :think …), { } for none; answers the reply, the message under :message
: ollama-chat ( model messages options -- reply )
	| model messages options |
	"POST" "chat" options { :model model :messages messages :stream :0 } merge ollama-request ;

\ the next message streamed: each reply handed to the handler ( reply -- ) as it arrives, its piece under :message; answers the final reply with :message the pieces gathered into one
: ollama-chat-streaming ( model messages options handler -- reply )
	| model messages options handler |

	"chat" options { :model model :messages messages } merge handler ollama-stream to replies

	replies last copy
	replies { :role "assistant" :content "" } ' ollama-add-piece reduce :message ! ;

\ === tools ===

\ the tools the conversations offer, each { :definition :handler }
[ ] to ollama-tool-list

\ register a tool: the function definition the model sees, { :name :description :parameters } with :parameters a JSON Schema object, and the word ( arguments -- output ) that runs it, given the arguments frame the model supplied and answering a string or a value sent as its JSON text
: ollama-add-tool ( definition handler -- )
	| definition handler |
	ollama-tool-list { :definition definition :handler handler } add-last! drop ;

\ forget every registered tool
: ollama-forget-tools ( -- )
	| ^ollama-tool-list |
	[ ] to ollama-tool-list ;

\ the registered tools as a chat request's :tools
: ollama-tools ( -- tools )
	ollama-tool-list ( entry | { :type "function" :function entry@definition } ) map ;

\ run a tool call a reply asked for, answering the tool message that carries its output: the registered handler for the call's function name, given the call's arguments. An unknown name, or a handler that throws, answers the error as the output, so the model reads it
: ollama-run-tool ( call -- message )
	| call |

	call@function to function
	function@name to name
	function :arguments { } @or to arguments
	ollama-tool-list ( entry | entry@definition@name name = ) find-first to entry

	entry null? if
		name "Error executing tool: no tool named {0}" format to output
	else
		( arguments entry@handler execute ) catch if
			dup frame? if :message @ then "Error executing tool: {0}" format
		then to output
	then
	output string? not if output frame>json to output then

	{ :role "tool" :tool_name name :content output } ;

\ a conversation: each prompt, a string taken as the user's or a message frame, added in turn and answered by a chat offering the registered tools; while a reply asks for tools they run, their messages are added and the model answers again. Answers the whole history, the model's and the tools' messages included
: ollama-converse ( model prompts options -- messages )
	| model prompts options |

	ollama-tool-list size 0 > if options { :tools ollama-tools } merge else options then to request-options
	[ ] to messages

	0 prompts size 1 do k
		prompts k @i to prompt
		messages prompt string? if :user prompt ollama-message else prompt then add-last! drop
		model messages request-options ollama-chat @message to answer
		messages answer add-last! drop

		begin answer :tool_calls [ ] @or size 0 > while
			messages answer@tool_calls ' ollama-run-tool map concat to messages
			model messages request-options ollama-chat @message to answer
			messages answer add-last! drop
		repeat
	loop

	messages ;

\ === embeddings ===

\ embeddings of the input, a string or an array of strings, as a matrix of one row per input; options a frame of the request's other fields (:truncate :dimensions :options …), { } for none
: ollama-embed ( model input options -- embeddings )
	| model input options |

	"POST" "embed" options { :model model :input input } merge ollama-request @embeddings to rows

	rows flatten rows size matrix ;

\ === the model store ===

\ the names of the models the server holds
: ollama-models ( -- names )
	"GET" "tags" null ollama-request @models ( @name ) map ;

\ the models loaded in memory, each a frame as the server reports it
: ollama-running ( -- models )
	"GET" "ps" null ollama-request @models ;

\ the server's version
: ollama-version ( -- version )
	"GET" "version" null ollama-request @version ;

\ a model's details: its modelfile, parameters, template, model info and capabilities
: ollama-model-info ( model -- info )
	| model |
	"POST" "show" { :model model } ollama-request ;

\ copy a model under a new name
: ollama-copy ( source destination -- )
	| source destination |
	"POST" "copy" { :source source :destination destination } ollama-request drop ;

\ delete a model and its data
: ollama-delete ( model -- )
	| model |
	"DELETE" "delete" { :model model } ollama-request drop ;

\ download a model from the registry, answering the final reply, :status success
: ollama-pull ( model -- reply )
	| model |
	"POST" "pull" { :model model :stream :0 } ollama-request ;

\ download a model with its progress streamed: each reply ( :status and, while a layer downloads, :total and :completed ) handed to the handler; answers the final reply, which must report success
: ollama-pull-streaming ( model handler -- reply )
	| model handler |
	"pull" { :model model } handler ollama-stream ollama-final-status ;

\ upload a model to the registry, answering the final reply
: ollama-push ( model -- reply )
	| model |
	"POST" "push" { :model model :stream :0 } ollama-request ;

\ upload a model with its progress streamed to the handler; answers the final reply, which must report success
: ollama-push-streaming ( model handler -- reply )
	| model handler |
	"push" { :model model } handler ollama-stream ollama-final-status ;

\ create a model: fields a frame of the request's other fields, :from an existing model or :files blobs by file name, and :system :template :parameters :quantize …; answers the final reply
: ollama-create ( model fields -- reply )
	| model fields |
	"POST" "create" fields { :model model :stream :0 } merge ollama-request ;

\ create a model with its progress streamed to the handler; answers the final reply, which must report success
: ollama-create-streaming ( model fields handler -- reply )
	| model fields handler |
	"create" fields { :model model } merge handler ollama-stream ollama-final-status ;

\ === blobs ===

\ a curl request whose body is not kept, answering the status; a failed transfer throws curl's message
: ollama-status-only ( arguments -- status )
	| arguments |

	[ "curl" "-sS" "-o" "/dev/null" "-w" "%{http_code}" ] arguments concat run-result to result
	result@status 0 = not if result@err trim throw then

	result@out string>number ; internal

\ a file's SHA-256 digest as the blob API names it, sha256:<hex>, from the shasum command
: ollama-file-digest ( path -- digest )
	| path |

	[ "shasum" "-a" "256" path ] run-result to result
	result@status 0 = not if result@err trim throw then

	result@out " " split first "sha256:" swap + ;

\ whether the server holds the blob with that digest
: ollama-blob? ( digest -- flag )
	| digest |
	[ "-I" ollama-url "blobs/" + digest + ] ollama-status-only 200 = ;

\ send a file to the server as a blob unless it holds one with the file's digest already; answers the digest
: ollama-push-blob ( path -- digest )
	| path |

	path ollama-file-digest to digest
	digest ollama-blob? if digest exit then

	[ "-T" path "-X" "POST" ollama-url "blobs/" + digest + ] ollama-status-only to status
	status 200 < status 300 >= or if status "" ollama-error throw then

	digest ;

\ create a model from a GGUF file: the file sent as a blob and named in :files by its file name, with the other fields in options; answers the final reply
: ollama-create-from-gguf ( model path options -- reply )
	| model path options |

	path ollama-push-blob to digest

	model options { :files { path basename string>symbol digest } } merge ollama-create ;

\ create a model from a safetensors directory: each regular file in it sent as a blob and named in :files by its file name, with the other fields in options; answers the final reply
: ollama-create-from-safetensors ( model directory options -- reply )
	| model directory options |

	{ } to files
	directory list-directory to names

	0 names size 1 do k
		directory "/" + names k @i + to path
		path file-info@kind :file = if
			files path ollama-push-blob names k @i string>symbol ! drop
		then
	loop

	model options { :files files } merge ollama-create ;
